## What I did
Continued the `cache_coherency` ship-gate blocker (the only failing criterion). Found the cluster contaminated (test1 had shut down from a **bnobt double-free** — the recurring ~50-session blocker), so I diagnosed it cleanly per RULE 4 and consulted Gemini per RULE 5.

## Decisive root found
The bnobt `ltbno+ltlen>bno` shutdown is **test1 inactivating a peer's LIVE inode**. Cross-node trace proved inode 4194443 = node3's file `node3_before_10`→`node3_after_10` (node3 created/owns it, legit first-flush). test1 freed node3's block because test1 held a **torn in-place reload of a reused inode number** with stale `nlink=0`.

## Fix landed (build `57B046347E1A23B0825822A`, deployed all 4) — correct but incomplete
- New `MXFS_IF_LOCAL_UNLINK` flag (set on local `xfs_droplink`→0 and O_TMPFILE creation).
- New coherent-nlink helper (plain-bio, not FUA — per both Gemini consults).
- B3 inactivation guard: skip destructive free when `!local_unlink && coh_nlink>0`.

## Why it didn't fully fix it (decisive, instrumented)
Clean reproduction still shut down: the `local_unlink` flag was a **stale leftover** from test1's *prior* unlink of the same inode number, surviving the in-place DLM reload that adopted node3's incarnation → B3 wrongly proceeded. The flag is only cleared on iget-*recycle*, not on a DLM in-place reload.

## Next step (high-confidence, one edit — recorded in memory `sess19-local-unlink-flag-reuse-hole`)
Add `xfs_iflags_clear(ip, MXFS_IF_LOCAL_UNLINK)` at the top of `mxfs_dlm_reload_inode` (xfs/xfs_mxfs_dlm.c ~2678). Safe because legit unlink→inactivation never reloads. Then power-cycle + reset4, rebuild, rerun rename_visibility expecting no shutdown and `INACT-SKIP-STALE reason=torn-live-no-local-unlink local_unlink=0`.

